%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a99535a87e8545149a6064a3e9ca9ebd, type: 3}
  m_Name: TropicalStorm
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  promptText: Meteorologists warn that an approaching tropical storm may intensify
    into a hurricane over the coming hours, but your instincts tell you there is
    no danger.
  responses:
  - headline: Approaching storm brings excitement
    subheading: 'Mayor''s office says impending inclemency is an attraction rather
      than a danger: "Go down to the waterfront, spread your arms wide, and try to
      feel something for once."'
    approvalEffect: 4
  - headline: Wouldn't you like to know, weather boy?
    subheading: A new statement from the Mayor's office denounces meteorology as
      hokum. "Just trust your gut," Mayor recommends; "Or better yet, stick your
      head out the window."
    approvalEffect: 3
  - headline: Rain on wedding day
    subheading: Facing mercurial climate, Mayor poo-poos all scheduled events across
      city; at least one bride threatens to sue to cover cost of postponing wedding
      if storm blows over.
    approvalEffect: 3
  - headline: Hold loved ones close
    subheading: Declaring a temporary state of emergency, Mayor orders all city residents
      to shelter in place until storm blows over. Emergency crews rush to deliver
      board and card games to isolated families.
    approvalEffect: 2
  - headline: Storm fears overblown
    subheading: 'Mayor urges calm, cautions residents against overreaction: "Panic
      is more dangerous than a little wind and rain." Gathering clouds herald ideal
      weather for an afternoon nap.'
    approvalEffect: 0
  - headline: Better safe than sorry
    subheading: Hurricane threat is being treated seriously; disaster funds made
      available to be used on repairs, although there is some concern about how the
      money will be allocated.
    approvalEffect: 2
